# Tracer: compare exact closed complex expressions only when real-valued.
# Before (rejected):
# i^2 < 0
# 0 < i^4
# Former behavior: the closed rational comparator did not reduce complex syntax.
# Now: zero imaginary coordinates permit exact real rational comparison.
i^2 < 0
0 > i^2
0 < i^4
i^4 > 0
i-i <= 0
i^2 $in R-

# Boundary: 0 <= i^2, 0 < i^2 and comparisons of nonreal values reject.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/atomic/by_builtin_rule/closed_complex_real_order.lit
# Implementation: rational_expression/decimal_comparison.rs; focused Rust controls.
